// Dust devils (WorldActorHandler, DustDevilPuff, DustDevilDebris): summoned with /dsactor as the warm-up starts, on a
// flat platform of sand built high over a desert, so no wall or water breaks them up and nothing else is in view. At
// night, so none start on their own: each run has only the summoned ones. Each is summoned with a fixed seed ("dsactor
// <kind> <n>"), so every run, on either platform, has the same ones (size, path, life; the held day gives the same
// wind), and the bigger run's first ones are the smaller run's. Four, as a few could be in view on a busy afternoon,
// and twelve, far more than ever start naturally. A dust devil lives 37 seconds at least: the warm-up and the recording
// fit in that. Facing east, downwind on the bench world's day (the time is held), so they travel away from the camera
// and stay in view: facing south they drifted out of it to the left, and their drawing went unmeasured. See README.md.
{
  "world": "bench",
  "seed": 20261030,
  "setup": [
    "gamemode creative",
    "gamerule advance_time false",
    "gamerule advance_weather false",
    "gamerule spawn_mobs false"
  ],
  "video": {
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080,
    "vsync": false,
